Overlay patch 0057: a harness hook that hands player one an item (VR R9,
item 5's artifact).

spec C8, "harness first": R9 needs a screenshot of the player's OWN triple
shells orbiting in first person, and of a trailing item behind the kart, to
prove 0056 actually made them visible. There is no cheat, no debug menu and no
item selector anywhere in this port, and driving 8th place round a GP hoping
for the right box is not a repeatable test — the suite would flake on the item
table's RNG rather than on the thing under test.

So: one shell-owned request word, consumed inside `check_player_use_item`.
`gSohVRDbgGrantItem` is an MK64 item id (defines.h ITEM_*); when it is >= 0 the
matching item ACTOR is spawned for player one through the game's own
`use_*_item` helpers — the same ones `player_use_item` calls — and the request
is cleared, so it fires ONCE per `vr set item <id>`.

Writing `player->currentItemCopy` does NOT work and the first draft of this
patch found out the hard way: `update_objects.c` re-syncs that field from the
HUD roulette object (`sp38->currentItemCopy = object->type;`) every single
frame, so the grant was overwritten before anything could read it. Spawning the
actor is both simpler and closer to the real thing.

Player one only (gPlayerOne), so it can never touch a CPU racer or a
split-screen player. -1, the default, does nothing at all, and it is the only
value that ever exists outside the dev console bridge, which is compiled out of
public builds (trap C7).

REV2 (VR R17-A item 2a): the MUSHROOMS. the user's 1.0.0.13 report is about what
he sees while a mushroom is running, and the suite has no way to make one
happen -- driving a GP hoping for the right item box is exactly the flake this
patch exists to avoid. MK64 does not spawn an actor for a mushroom: the whole
of `use item` for the four mushroom ids is `player->triggers |= SHROOM_TRIGGER`
(actors_extended.c's own switch, a few lines below this hook), which is what
raises `boostPower` past the 2.0 that gates the boost-flash kart quad. Same
one-shot, same player-one gate, same helper the game uses.


--- a/src/racing/actors_extended.c
+++ b/src/racing/actors_extended.c
@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
+#ifdef __IOS__
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0057, VR R9 harness): an item id to hand player one, or
+// -1 for "do nothing". Consumed (and reset to -1) in check_player_use_item.
+// Declared at the head of the file, outside overlay 0053's hunk context.
+extern volatile int gSohVRDbgGrantItem;
+#endif
 #include <libultraship.h>
 #include <macros.h>
 #include <defines.h>
@@ -972,6 +978,48 @@
                 }
             }
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+            // SOH_IOS (overlay 0057, VR R9 harness): grant player one an item
+            // on request. Placed here rather than at the head of the loop
+            // body because overlay 0053 owns that spot and a patch must never
+            // land inside another patch's hunk context. -1 (the default, and
+            // the only value outside the dev console bridge) does nothing.
+            if ((player == gPlayerOne) && (gSohVRDbgGrantItem >= 0)) {
+                s16 sohItem = (s16) gSohVRDbgGrantItem;
+                gSohVRDbgGrantItem = -1;
+                // Spawn the item ACTOR directly rather than writing
+                // player->currentItemCopy: the item window's update
+                // (update_objects.c) re-syncs that field from the HUD
+                // roulette object EVERY frame, so a write there is gone
+                // before anything can use it. These are the same helpers
+                // player_use_item calls, so the resulting state is the
+                // real thing and not a mock-up.
+                switch (sohItem) {
+                    case ITEM_TRIPLE_GREEN_SHELL:
+                        use_triple_shell_item(player, ACTOR_TRIPLE_GREEN_SHELL);
+                        break;
+                    case ITEM_TRIPLE_RED_SHELL:
+                        use_triple_shell_item(player, ACTOR_TRIPLE_RED_SHELL);
+                        break;
+                    case ITEM_GREEN_SHELL:
+                        use_green_shell_item(player);
+                        break;
+                    case ITEM_BANANA:
+                        use_banana_item(player);
+                        break;
+                    // rev2 (R17-A item 2a): the mushrooms. No actor --
+                    // MK64 raises a trigger and the boost follows.
+                    case ITEM_MUSHROOM:
+                    case ITEM_DOUBLE_MUSHROOM:
+                    case ITEM_TRIPLE_MUSHROOM:
+                    case ITEM_SUPER_MUSHROOM:
+                        player->triggers |= SHROOM_TRIGGER;
+                        break;
+                    default:
+                        break;
+                }
+            }
+#endif
             if (((player->type & PLAYER_HUMAN) != 0) && (player->currentItemCopy != ITEM_NONE) &&
                 ((player->type & PLAYER_START_SEQUENCE) == 0)) {
                 if ((controller->buttonPressed & Z_TRIG) != 0) {
